# --- Project data (NEVER commit market data or credentials) ---
data/raw/
data/snapshots/
data/cache/
# `data/curated/` and `data/ledger/` are excluded by CONTENTS rather than as
# directories. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is excluded,
# and three small files under these two are the whole point of the
# reproducibility work -- see the negations further down.
data/curated/*
data/ledger/*
logs/
*.parquet
*.duckdb
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# --- Secrets ---
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/secrets.yaml
config/parameters.local.yaml

# --- OS / editors ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# runtime state
data/jobs.sqlite3
.claude/
data/curated/.store.lock

# --- Provenance: the three files that must be committed -----------------------
# `data/curated/` and `data/ledger/` are excluded above and must stay excluded:
# they hold a quarter of a gigabyte of market data and the run ledger. But three
# small files under them are the whole point of the reproducibility work, and an
# ignore rule that swallowed them would leave every result unable to name its
# own inputs -- which is finding D1.
!data/curated/MANIFEST.json
!data/curated/trial_registry.jsonl
!data/ledger/epochs.jsonl
# Belt and braces: a stray parquet under either must never be re-included by
# one of the negations above.
data/curated/**/*.parquet
data/ledger/**/*.parquet

# --- Research caches: derived, large, and reconstructable ---------------------
# `work/*.py` rebuilds every one of these from the store in about eight minutes,
# and `work/cache/panels.pkl` alone is 134 MB. A repository that carries derived
# binaries is a repository whose history cannot be cloned.
work/cache/
work/cache_v1/
work/*.log

# --- Build and audit artifacts. These were committed once and should not be
# again: a tarball of the source, a git bundle of the same history, and a PDF
# render of a report that lives in docs/ are three copies of things the repo
# already holds, and they are 1.1 MB that every clone pays for.
*.tar.gz
*.bundle
ProSignal-Audit.pdf

# Audit experiment caches (large, regenerable)
research/v3/experiments/*.pkl
research/v3/experiments/panel_*.parquet
